### Kippu walkthrough — run the requests from top to bottom (RustRover / IntelliJ HTTP client).
#
# Prepare keys and start the server first, as described in docs/walkthrough.md, then fill in
# the three values below. Every other id is captured from the responses as you go.

@base = http://localhost:8080
# Output of: kippu root-token --config kippu.toml --key root.key --name owner   (valid 10 min)
@root_token = paste-the-root-token-here
# Contents of attestor.pub (from: kippu keygen --out attestor)
@attestor_public_key = paste-attestor.pub-here

### 1. Root creates an organization
POST {{base}}/v1/admin/organizations
Authorization: Bearer {{root_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slug": "comiket", "name": "Comic Market" }

> {% client.global.set("organization_id", response.body.id); %}

### 2. Root creates an organizer account
POST {{base}}/v1/admin/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{root_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "staff@example.org",
  "password": "correct horse battery",
  "display_name": "Staff",
  "role": "organizer"
}

> {% client.global.set("organizer_id", response.body.id); %}

### 3. … and makes it a member of the organization (204)
PUT {{base}}/v1/admin/organizations/{{organization_id}}/members/{{organizer_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{root_token}}

### 4. The organizer signs in
POST {{base}}/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "staff@example.org", "password": "correct horse battery" }

> {% client.global.set("organizer_token", response.body.access_token.token); %}

### 5. The organizer creates an event (a draft)
POST {{base}}/v1/organizations/{{organization_id}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{organizer_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slug": "c110",
  "title": "Comic Market 110",
  "venue": "Tokyo Big Sight",
  "starts_at": "2027-08-16T10:00:00+09:00",
  "ends_at": "2027-08-17T16:00:00+09:00"
}

> {% client.global.set("event_id", response.body.id); %}

### 6. … opens a sale for it (open admission: no waiting room)
POST {{base}}/v1/events/{{event_id}}/sales
Authorization: Bearer {{organizer_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "General",
  "opens_at": "2026-10-01T00:00:00Z",
  "closes_at": "2027-08-01T00:00:00Z"
}

> {% client.global.set("sale_id", response.body.id); %}

### 7. … and adds a ticket type. Extension 128 is printed on every ticket.
POST {{base}}/v1/sales/{{sale_id}}/ticket-types
Authorization: Bearer {{organizer_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Day 1",
  "price": { "amount_minor": 2500, "currency": "JPY" },
  "capacity": 100,
  "valid_from": "2027-08-16T08:00:00+09:00",
  "valid_until": "2027-08-17T00:00:00+09:00",
  "ticket_extensions": { "128": "EAST-1" }
}

> {% client.global.set("ticket_type_id", response.body.id); %}

### 8. Root registers a payment attestor with its public key
POST {{base}}/v1/admin/attestors
Authorization: Bearer {{root_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Card gateway",
  "environment": "live",
  "keys": [{ "key_id": "k1", "public_key": "{{attestor_public_key}}" }]
}

> {% client.global.set("attestor_id", response.body.id); %}

### 9. The organizer accepts the attestor for the sale: PATCH sends only what changes
PATCH {{base}}/v1/sales/{{sale_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{organizer_token}}
Content-Type: application/merge-patch+json

{ "version": 1, "accepted_attestors": ["{{attestor_id}}"] }

### 10. … and publishes the event
PATCH {{base}}/v1/events/{{event_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{organizer_token}}
Content-Type: application/merge-patch+json

{ "version": 1, "status": "published" }

### 11. A buyer signs up
POST {{base}}/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "miku@example.org", "password": "correct horse battery", "display_name": "Miku" }

### 12. … and signs in
POST {{base}}/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "miku@example.org", "password": "correct horse battery" }

> {% client.global.set("buyer_token", response.body.access_token.token); %}

### 13. Anyone can browse published events
GET {{base}}/v1/events

### 14. The buyer asks for two tickets (202; send it again and nothing changes)
POST {{base}}/v1/sales/{{sale_id}}/purchase-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{buyer_token}}
Idempotency-Key: my-first-order
Content-Type: application/json

{ "items": [{ "ticket_type_id": "{{ticket_type_id}}", "quantity": 2 }] }

> {% client.global.set("purchase_request", response.headers.valueOf("Location")); %}

### 15. A background worker reserves the tickets: poll until the status is `reserved`
GET {{base}}{{purchase_request}}
Authorization: Bearer {{buyer_token}}

> {% client.global.set("reservation_id", response.body.reservation_id); %}

### 16. The buyer chooses to pay through the attestor (`payment_pending`)
POST {{base}}/v1/reservations/{{reservation_id}}/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{buyer_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "attestor_id": "{{attestor_id}}" }

# Now report the payment as the attestor would; see step 17 in docs/walkthrough.md.

### 18. The buyer's tickets, signed
GET {{base}}/v1/me/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{buyer_token}}

### 19. The keys a gate trusts
GET {{base}}/.well-known/kippu/ticket-keys
